  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Marine Monitoring Along the Aqaba Coastline (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the Phase I assessment of marine monitoring along the Aqaba coastline and laying the foundation for the next phase of ASEZA&#x2019;s 25-year monitoring programme, Phase II focuses on implementing the recommended upgrades over a three-year period.The project strengthens the Norway&#x2013;Jordan partnership, in collaboration with the Institute of Marine Research (IMR) and other regional and international institutions, by deploying advanced technologies, including AI-based analysis, across five core workstreams: oceanography and water quality, fisheries assessment, benthic habitat mapping, data management, and a pilot marine pollution early warning system. The introduction of real-time sensors, coupled with institutional standard operating procedures (SOPs), will significantly enhance ASEZA&#x2019;s capacity for risk-informed marine governance.Key deliverables include fisheries management plans, maps for the conservation of vulnerable marine ecosystems (VMEs), an integrated marine data platform, and comprehensive capacity-building programmes. In parallel, the project will pilot an integrated early warning system with real-time pollution monitoring and establish SOPs for pollution response. Collectively, these efforts aim to safeguard the Gulf of Aqaba&#x2019;s coral reef climate refugium while advancing a sustainable blue economy and reinforcing Jordan&#x2019;s regional leadership</narrative>
  </description>
